  "question": "The database is a software project management system primarily designed to manage the development process of software projects, task assignments for team members, code submissions, and project version management. The key tables involved in the system include: User Table, Project Table, Project Version Table, Task Table, Code Submission Table. Below is a brief description of the database function.\n\n1.User Management:   \nRecords the basic information of each user in the system, who may be a project manager, developer, or tester.  \nFields: User ID, User Name, Password, Email, Phone, Role, Registration Time, Last Login Time\n\n2.Project Management: \nRecords the basic information of software development projects, each project has a responsible person and manages its current status.  \nFields: Project ID, Project Name, Project Introduction, Responsible Person ID, Creation Time, Project Status\n\n3. Project Version Management:\nRecords the version information of each project, including version number, release date, etc. Each version is associated with a specific project.  \nFields: Version ID, Project ID, Version Name, Release Date, Version Description, Is Stable Version\n\n4. Task Management:\nRecords the assignment and progress of tasks within the project; tasks are the work that developers need to complete. Each task has a start time, end time, and task status.  \nFields: Project ID, Assigned To User ID, Task Name, Task Status, Start Time, End Time, Task Description\n\n5. Code Submission Management:  \nRecords the code information submitted by developers to the project, including submission time, submission description, code path, etc.  \nFields: User ID, Project ID, Submission Time, Submission Description, Code Path",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0422\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `project_introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `responsible_person_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `project_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`),\n  KEY `responsible_person_id` (`responsible_person_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`responsible_person_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project_version` (\n  `version_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `version_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `version_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_stable_version` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`version_id`),\n  KEY `project_id` (`project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `project_version_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assigned_to_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `task_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `task_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`),\n  KEY `project_id` (`project_id`),\n  KEY `assigned_to_user_id` (`assigned_to_user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `task_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`assigned_to_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `code_submission` (\n  `submission_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `submission_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `submission_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `code_path` varchar(500) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`submission_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `project_id` (`project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `code_submission_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `code_submission_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
